{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996086-auspex-vs-auspex","id":996086,"title":"Auspex vs. Auspex","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-31T08:37:15-07:00","id":996086,"title":"Auspex vs. Auspex","content":"Hi all,<br /> Normally if someone uses Auspex can't be detected. But I'm wondering if someone else with Auspex, the victim himself or a third one, could use one of the firsts 2 powers to ask if is there someone using Auspex in the room. Exactly as is allowed to ask if someone is using auspex 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T09:36:11-07:00","id":996118,"title":"","content":"I think the problem is that the first three levels of Auspex have no duration. When you ask if anyone is using Auspex they've already gotten their answers and isn't using the power anymore.<br /> When it comes to Auspex 4 it's instead a matter of what limits the ST has put on Auspex. Are you able to ask about what disciplines other vampires have active at all if they're not external? It's up to the ST, but I'd disallow it.<br /> In our group we use an updated version of the devotion Arcane Sight (Auspex 2, any Blood Sorcery 1) to both reveal supernatural effects with Auspex 1-3, and target supernatural effects with Auspex 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T09:37:50-07:00","id":996119,"title":"","content":"I allow all kindred to potentially detect a Level 5 if he crosses through the range of detection with a generic perception check. But they don't know who or what they saw. (Usually I describe it as a strange human shaped distortion or greyish white ghostlike form with no distinguishing details. And ghosts are definitely existing &quot;things&quot; in my setting.) Auspex Level 2 or 3 would potentially auto reveal Level 5 user if the question is appropriately worded and Level 5 is currently in the vicinity. No Clash of Wills. If the Level 5 is also employing Obfuscate then a clash of wills is involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T11:22:39-07:00","id":996159,"title":"","content":"Hm, using Auspex is instantaneous, true. That said, I see no reason why level 2 couldn't allow you to determine if someone possesses Auspex. It woudn't necessarily allow you to know if they used it (although it's usually probable) or what level they have in it (although why not a general indication of whether they're good at it or not), but detecting an Auspex user doesn't seem absurd. It'd probably have to be a precise question, not just &quot;what kind of powers does this guy have ?&quot; but more like &quot;does that vampire have Auspex?&quot;.<br /> <br /> Or you could roll for the level 2, asking what disciplines they have and each success identifies a discipline. To avoid making it overpowered, it'd be better to play on the vague nature of the visions. Less subtle disciplines like the physical ones would be more obvious (vampire looks totally ripped from a certain angle, their skin looks rough like stone, their movement feels too quick to be natural...), the rest less so. The more exotic disciplines would give weirder info making them unidentifiable if you don't know it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T11:55:49-07:00","id":996185,"title":"","content":"I had an idea once for an Auspex/Obfuscate devotion called The Jig is Up; once per scene, a character can automatically recognize when they've been made (being somewhere they shouldn't, doing something they shouldn't) the instant it happens. If the observer has Obfuscate or Auspex, it becomes a clash of wills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T12:41:22-07:00","id":996212,"title":"","content":"Ok I'm going to explain better my problem. <br /> I don't want to spoiler beacause I'm using NPC from the official setting new orleans (but with rules and systems of second edition) so I just say: a PC with Auspex could, in any social event like Elysium or other, have a good chance to read memory of some BIG CHARACTER and know her deep secrets. Or even with auspex 2 he could know things like diablerie or stuffs like that. <br /> Now, it's a real big problem for the story to know too soon secrets of this weight. I just wondered if, in an Elysium for example, someone could know if this character is using Auspex (1,2 or 4), on who and maybe alerts the NPC; or maybe is the NPC himself to try to detect it. <br /> I really have problems to handle Auspex in this situations <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> I mean, if I use Majesty/dominate there is always the chance to be detected so it could be a deterrent, but with Auspex it's to easy to use without any chance to be detected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 10-31-2016, 03:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T12:43:16-07:00","id":996213,"title":"","content":"This is why vampires are paranoid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T12:53:06-07:00","id":996220,"title":"","content":"So first of all, no, there's not really a way to detect if someone is using Auspex 1 or 2 by the rules as written. That said, you could always make something up, like a Devotion or Bloodline Gift that allows it. Maybe the Keeper of Elysium has a special Devotion involving Auspex and Animalism that pings her spidey senses whenever someone uses a Discipline in her territory.<br /> <br /> Second of all, it sounds like your primary concern is with characters finding out NPCs secrets &quot;too soon.&quot; But how do you define &quot;too soon?&quot; What makes this particular Elysium gathering an inappropriate time for the PCs to be able to learn this information? What is the appropriate time for them to learn it, and what makes it appropriate?<br /> <br /> In my opinion, there's no such thing as information being revealed &quot;too soon.&quot; I am creating a story <i>with</i> my players, not <i>for</i> them, and the moment they use their characters' abilities and their own ingenuity to uncover a piece of information is precisely the moment they were &quot;supposed&quot; to discover it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 10-31-2016, 04:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T13:02:39-07:00","id":996223,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of that devotion!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T13:14:45-07:00","id":996226,"title":"","content":"That, basically.<br /> <br /> Plus, I guess that depends on the GM, but to me, Auspex 4, when it comes to digging memoeires, is only useful if you kind of know what you're looking for. You're usually not gonna get big secrets by looking randomly into their mind. You're just as likely to stumble upon the memory of their last meal or that they came close to frenzy yesterday when they stuck their little toe while being low on blood.<br /> <br /> The more passive aspect of monitoring their mind is more problematic, but not hopeless either : &quot;...the vampire can discern the victim\u2019s precise mood and intention, and some snippets of her current motivation and considerations.&quot; Obviously, if the players are being total douchebags and, say, plan to use auspex 4 on every important vampire in the elyseum for half an hour until nobody's left, they might stumble upon something interesting. Without that, they would have to be at least a little lucky to get really sensitive information.<br /> <br /> As a security measure, smart vampires might only want to socialize superficially in the main parts of the elyseum, but get behind closed doors when they want to discuss private or important business. An important elyseum will also have security. Some of that security might be vampires or ghouls with auspex that make sure nobody's using telepathy to ruin the party. Whether this is made public or not is up to you (vampires might not trust the security to be neutral and suspect them of fishing for their secrets), but maybe the vampires the players want to spy on are on good terms with the owner of the elyseum and would be warned if the players were caught looking into their brain.<br /> <br /> Finally, a rare Auspex + Resilience devotion could justify a higher resistance to Auspex 4, and if you want something kinda legit, there's the Ordo Dracul merit series &quot;mind of the...&quot; which, at level 3 makes it harder to do stuff to your mind. You could also have Indomitable, but if you read the merit, it's only a penalty to powers that &quot;influence&quot; your mind, but if you want to broaden it to telepathy, eh, why not I'd say.<br /> <br /> <br /> So no, there is no good solution since you can't ban something if you don't know it's being used, but imaginative vampires will try to limit the risks by being careful, laying traps, having allies to have their back, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T16:47:27-07:00","id":996321,"title":"","content":"So, would a question with auspex 1 like: &quot;who here is most likely to steal secrets with Auspex&quot; be legit? <br /> <br /> And once restricted the ring, what about the question with auspex 2 like: &quot;did he use Auspex on someone? Or is he using auspex?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T11:18:29-08:00","id":1000902,"title":"","content":"I think part of the solution is to dial back expectations for Auspex 4. If it can <i><b>casually</b></i> function as a deep mind-reading power then why would vampires gather at all? As S. Brechen points out it is keyed to surface thoughts, so if you wander through the Elysium with it on then you'll pick up whatever people are thinking about at the moment, especially stuff like &quot;t<i>hat Shadow's looking at me again, probably reading my mind--F you little bitch!</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> But the natural impulse of the human mind when asked a question or reminded of something is to spring to a related memory, even if we don't say it immediately and can control non-verbal reactions. You want to get the <i>best</i> good out of Auspex? Use it while springing a trap on your target, poking them to remind them of something or asking a question with double-meaning. It takes a lot of will to not even <i>think</i> of an incriminating response to &quot;so, when will you stop beating your ghoul?&quot; (Or, whatever.)<br /> <br /> But asking these questions socially, out loud, means playing the harpy game and opening yourself or others up for analysis. That's part of the fun. If you're not asking them socially then you've got your target in a controlled environment--possibly one they cannot just leave from, and you can afford to probe repeatedly until you get the deeper memories you want.<br /> <br /> <b>[Talking to handcuffed and duct-tape-gagged subject.]</b><br /> &quot;So, glad to meet you--my name is Buttercup. Shake! No...?&quot; (<i>I'm Niell</i>)<br /> &quot;Ok Niell, let's relax while we're waiting for the boss. Where do you work?&quot; (<i>The F--- get out!</i>)<br /> &quot;Sex work Niell? The wife approve?&quot; (<i>&lt;flash of an office&gt;Barbara!</i>)<br /> &quot;Don't worry, you'll be with Barbara soon. So what do you do for the office? Handle money?&quot; (<i>&lt;papers, folders, pictures&gt;No!</i>)<br /> &quot;Where do you file them, Niell. A trash can? Haha. No--you do important work. They go in a safe, don't they Niell.&quot; (<i>&lt;safe, trashcan, safe, keypad!&gt;</i>)<br /> &quot;What is the frequency, Kenneth! Sorry--Niell, there are numbers on the safe. Safe numbers. You like... 7!&quot; (<i>What? Safe... nine.</i>)<br /> &quot;Nine. Seven.&quot; (<i>Nine three two nine, idio.... shit.</i>)<br /> Whips out smartphone, tapping a text. &quot;Thanks Niell.&quot;<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T11:55:44-08:00","id":1000918,"title":"","content":"Question 1<br /> <br /> For me, provided the question is worded within character context, yes. The character would get a quick visual flash of the nearest Auspex user currently using Auspex or planning to use Auspex.<br /> <br /> Question 2<br /> <br /> For me, that question is too broad and has to be phrased within an in character context. You'd need to be more specific about when and which power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T04:55:46-08:00","id":1001312,"title":"","content":"If you absolutely, positively need to make elysium secure against auspex you can use a Purified. They basically have Unseen Sense [Power Use]. I vaguely recall that being a thing they explicitly do.<br /> <br /> Purified are in the Immortals book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T09:51:13-08:00","id":1001389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/996086-auspex-vs-auspex?p=996220#post996220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second of all, it sounds like your primary concern is with characters finding out NPCs secrets &quot;too soon.&quot; But how do you define &quot;too soon?&quot; What makes this particular Elysium gathering an inappropriate time for the PCs to be able to learn this information? What is the appropriate time for them to learn it, and what makes it appropriate?<br /> <br /> In my opinion, there's no such thing as information being revealed &quot;too soon.&quot; I am creating a story <i>with</i> my players, not <i>for</i> them, and the moment they use their characters' abilities and their own ingenuity to uncover a piece of information is precisely the moment they were &quot;supposed&quot; to discover it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree here. One important thing to consider is if starting characters can do it then its pretty safe to assume everyone else who has the ability has done it. In fact you might have one of the PC get a speech from a Mentor with Auspex that goes like this:<br /> <br /> &quot;So I know you're excited about your new found abilities but please be considerate that many others have them as well and that you aren't that original to ask questions we haven't thought up. For example half the elders in our city are Diablerists and have some fairly foul habits but dare mention any of that to anyone, even me, and we'll have to either figuratively or (depending on who you accuse), literally burn you at the stake. See our society is built on shaky alliances framed on a foundation of petty blackmails. Only new secrets count, anything that is old business we all pretend doesn't exist otherwise they'll bring up our dirty old secrets. I don't expect you to be wise enough to know which secrets are new or old, but I do expect you to not be an idiot when it comes to opening your mouth about any of it. I've chosen you as a companion to chum around with and share my wisdom, please don't make me be the one to put you down like a rabid dog for the mistake of thinking yourself wiser than you are.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}